# Phase 3 retest 1 (commit 18b3482) - D-2 DB verification after 25 concurrency runs
# Source: e2e-p3-concurrency-retest1-repeat25.log (25/25 passed), request title 'Race', one request per run.
# Each run: 10 parallel classify_request('included') then 12 parallel calls cycling additional/needs_clarification/included.
# Query (superuser, execute_sql): per request, classification events ordered by seq:
#   chain_ok          = every from equals the previous to (first from = unclassified)
#   seq_eq_created    = row_number() by seq equals row_number() by (created_at, seq)
#   created_strict    = created_at strictly increasing in seq order
#   last_ok           = last event (by seq) 'to' equals requests.classification
#   seq_unique        = no duplicate seq
#   contention_evidence = requests.updated_at (= now() of the LAST applying transaction, i.e. its start time)
#                         is earlier than the created_at of the previous event: that transaction started before the
#                         previous change was written and waited on the row lock (the D-2 trigger condition).
#   dup_rows          = identical (entity, metadata, created_at) rows
requests=25 class_events=243 min_ev_per_request=7 max_ev_per_request=12
chain_ok=25/25 seq_eq_created=25/25 created_strict=25/25 last_ok=25/25 seq_unique=25/25
request.created events=25 (one per request) dup_rows=0
contention_evidence=4/25 (lower bound: only the final transaction of each run can be checked this way)
